---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { render, legal, byName } from "../lib/md";
import { BUILDS, LAYERS } from "../data/firmware";
import { site } from "../config";
const warning = render(byName(legal, "firmware-warning.md")).html;
---
<Base title="Firmware" description="Download the FX Unleashed wheel app for the Simagic FX Pro, install it in a few simple steps, and go back to stock whenever you like.">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Firmware</p>
    <h1>The <span class="red">wheel app</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Unleashed mode needs our version of the wheel's own small program. Download it here, then follow the install steps: about 10 minutes, and Simagic's original is always one reinstall away.</p>

    <div class="warning prose" role="note" id="risks">
      <p class="eyebrow">Read this first</p>
      <Fragment set:html={warning} />
    </div>

    <div class="get card" id="get-it">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Newest wheel app</p>
        <h2 data-fw-build>The wheel app</h2>
        <p class="meta"><span data-fw-file>FXUnleashed-wheelapp</span> · <span data-fw-size>one small file</span> · for the FX Pro, wheel app 1.3.11</p>
      </div>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" data-fw-download href={site.firmwareReleases}>Download</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/start/#1-install-the-wheel-app">Install steps</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="next muted">The <a href="/start/#1-install-the-wheel-app">install guide</a> goes on from here with the plugin and the screen's RAM patch (picture memory): optional, but highly recommended. One guide, start to finish.</p>

    <h2 id="back-to-stock">Back to stock</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <ol>
        <li>Make sure Simagic's original file is back in SimPro's wheel folder (the last step of the install).</li>
        <li>Wheel on the base, base on, USB cable in. In SimPro open Device, FX Pro, Firmware and reinstall wheel app 1.3.11.</li>
        <li>Wait until SimPro says it's done. If it hangs after the wheel enters boot mode, close SimPro, start it again and reinstall.</li>
        <li>That's Simagic's own app again. The plugin's Wheel tab then shows no patch build.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <h2 class="curious">For the curious</h2>
    <p class="muted">None of this is needed to install it. It's here for anyone who wants to know exactly what they're putting on their wheel.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <details>
        <summary>What this file is</summary>
        <p>Simagic's own wheel app 1.3.11 with our changes. It is Simagic's software, shared by a community project without Simagic's involvement, and it may be taken down, so keep a copy. We never publish the key that protects Simagic's firmware, anywhere.</p>
        <p>It only changes the wheel's own app (lights, screen, buttons, USB). Your base and force feedback aren't involved.</p>
      </details>

      <details id="check">
        <summary>Check your download</summary>
        <p>The file's fingerprint (SHA-256) and size, read from the release itself:</p>
        <p><code data-fw-file>FXUnleashed-wheelapp</code><br /><code data-fw-bytes>(shown on the release page)</code><br /><code data-fw-sha>(shown on the release page)</code></p>
        <p>To check yours, open PowerShell in the folder with the file and run <code>Get-FileHash .\FXUnleashed-wheelapp-*.sfu</code>. The result must match exactly. If it doesn't, don't use the file.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Make it yourself from your own SimPro copy</summary>
        <p>The <a href={site.firmwareRepo}>firmware repository</a> has a patch tool. It checks that your copy of the wheel app in SimPro's folder is Simagic's original, applies our changes and checks the result against the same checksum, so you get identical bytes. Either way you install through SimPro, exactly as you would a firmware update, and then put Simagic's original back. Its <a href={`${site.firmwareRepo}/blob/main/docs/install.md`}>guide</a> has the steps.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What each build changes</summary>
        <div class="timeline">
          {BUILDS.map(b => (
            <div class={`build ${b.status}`}>
              <span class="n">{b.n}</span>
              <div><h3>{b.title} <span class="st">{b.status}</span></h3><p>{b.text}</p></div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How every build is checked</summary>
        <ol class="layers">
          {LAYERS.map(l => (
            <li>
              <span class="ring" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <div><h3>{l.title}</h3><p>{l.text}</p></div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<script src="../scripts/firmware.ts"></script>
<style>
  .page { padding: 150px 0 100px; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .warning { margin: 40px 0 36px; padding: 28px 30px; border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 176, 0, 0.35); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,176,0,0.07), rgba(255,176,0,0.02)); max-width: none; }
  .warning :global(p), .warning :global(li) { color: var(--text); }
  .warning .eyebrow { color: var(--amber); }
  .warning .eyebrow::before { background: var(--amber); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--amber); }
  .get { display: flex; gap: 24px; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 28px 30px; border-color: rgba(255, 31, 45, 0.4); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,31,45,0.08), var(--panel-solid)); }
  .get h2 { margin: 6px 0 8px; font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px); text-transform: none; }
  .get .meta { margin: 0; color: var(--text-3); font-size: 14px; }
  .get .actions { margin: 0; display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  h2 { margin-top: 70px; }
  .get h2 { margin-top: 6px; }
  .curious { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .next { margin-top: 18px; }
  .next a { color: var(--red-2); border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 90, 100, 0.35); }
  .layers { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 18px 0; display: grid; gap: 14px; counter-reset: l; }
  .layers li { display: flex; gap: 18px; padding: 18px; border-radius: 16px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .ring { flex: none; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid var(--red); box-shadow: 0 0 20px var(--red-glow), inset 0 0 12px var(--red-glow); position: relative; }
  .ring::after { counter-increment: l; content: counter(l); position: absolute; inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center; font: 700 17px var(--display); }
  .layers h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .layers p { margin: 0; }
  .timeline { position: relative; margin: 18px 0 18px 12px; padding-left: 30px; border-left: 2px solid var(--line); display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .build { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: flex-start; position: relative; }
  .build::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: -38px; top: 14px; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--green); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--green); }
  .build.next::before { background: var(--amber); box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--amber); }
  .n { font: 700 40px/1 var(--display); color: var(--red); min-width: 46px; }
  .build h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .build p { margin: 0; }
  .st { font: 700 10px/1 var(--display); letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: rgba(33,224,122,0.12); color: var(--green); vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 8px; }
  .next .st { background: rgba(255,176,0,0.12); color: var(--amber); }
</style>
